---
// About page — Will Wollack, the expanded founder story (blue/cobalt theme).
// The landing page compresses the story; this page expands it. Product
// detail lives on /journeyman (the "Rust & Iron" variant page).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  organization,
  personWillWollack,
  aboutPage,
  breadcrumbAbout,
} from '../lib/schema';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Will Wollack — Wollack Systems"
  description="Who is Will Wollack? The founder story: why he's building Wollack Systems, how networking and hustling landed cofounder Ethan Davidson, and why the mission can't wait."
  path="/about"
  jsonLd={[organization(), personWillWollack(), aboutPage(), breadcrumbAbout()]}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Wollack Systems</p>
      <h1>
        The founder is a field man who decided the knowledge shouldn't die on schedule.
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Will Wollack didn't come to manufacturing through a spreadsheet. He came through the room
        &mdash; trade events, shop tours, chamber mixers, cold handshakes &mdash; and kept hearing
        the same sentence everywhere:
        <strong>the knowledge that runs this plant is one retirement from gone.</strong>
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:willwollack@gmail.com?subject=Walkthrough%20request"
          >Book a walkthrough</a
        >
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/journeyman">See what he's building</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who he is -->
  <section class="section section-tinted" id="who">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Who is Will Wollack?</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Will Wollack is the founder of Wollack Systems and the voice of Journeyman. He builds the
        old way: show up, network, hustle. Wherever the people who make things gather, he's in the
        room &mdash; and he listens for the moment a plant manager mentions the repair nobody could
        explain, or the machinist nobody can replace.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        He isn't chasing software for its own sake. He's building something real: a permanent
        record of the expertise that keeps American plants running, captured from the people who
        hold it &mdash; while it can still be captured.
      </p>
      <div class="accent-callout">
        <p>
          He heard the problem in every room he ever pitched in. So he stopped pitching the problem
          and started building the record.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why he's building it -->
  <section class="section" id="why">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Why he's building it</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        The mission is written into the company's bones: record what your best people know &mdash;
        without asking them to touch a computer &mdash; so the plant keeps knowing what they knew,
        after they're gone.
      </p>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact-number">&asymp;1/3</div>
          <p>of US manufacturing workers are over 55 &mdash; and heading for the exit together.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact-number">800 yrs</div>
          <p>
            of trades, and the transfer method never changed: stand next to someone until you can
            do it too.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact-number">First time</div>
          <p>
            AI can finally learn from a recording of someone explaining their work. But it cannot
            go get it. That part takes us.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="section-close">
        When the best troubleshooter on the floor retires, the line runs slower, scrap goes up
        &mdash; and nobody can say why. The people who know are still alive and still reachable.
        That won't last.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it's being built -->
  <section class="section section-tinted" id="how">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How: hustle first, then the record.</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Show up. Pitch. Repeat.</h3>
          <p>
            Will does the unscalable thing on purpose &mdash; face to face. Networking events,
            plant walkthroughs, conversations standing next to the machine. The pitch is one
            sentence long: your best people are retiring, and what they know leaves with them
            unless somebody writes it down.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>One pitch found a cofounder.</h3>
          <p>
            At a networking event in Newport Beach, California, Will pitched Journeyman to
            <a class="inline-link" href="https://etok.me/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ethan Davidson</a>
            &mdash; software engineer, formerly of Google, now building Wazoo. Ethan signed on as
            cofounder, and now builds the AI that turns shop-floor talk into a written record.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Build something real.</h3>
          <p>
            No slideware, no someday: Journeyman captures real experts on real floors, and every
            record belongs to the plant that paid for it. Wollack Systems grows one expert, one
            plant, one honest conversation at a time.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The work -->
  <section class="section" id="work">
    <div class="container pricing-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The work</p>
      <p class="price-anchor"><strong>Journeyman is the flagship.</strong></p>
      <p class="price-sub">
        Wollack Systems records what your best people know &mdash; hands-free &mdash; and turns it
        into a written, searchable record your plant owns. Journeyman is the product that does it.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row cta-center">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/journeyman">See how Journeyman works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="section section-paper" id="book">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Meet the man behind the mission.</h2>
      <p class="section-close-ink">
        One conversation with Will tells you what knowledge capture would look like for your floor.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row cta-center">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:willwollack@gmail.com?subject=Walkthrough%20request"
          >Book a walkthrough</a
        >
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://etok.me/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >Meet the cofounder</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Page-scoped: inline text links inside step copy on the dark ground. */
  .inline-link {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-accent-blue);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .inline-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-blue);
  }
</style>
